How does the linker do the stub replacement for a member like this?  This construct will be compiled down to something like:
```C#
private static readonly bool <>_isSupported;

static /*beforefieldinit*/ EventSource
{
    <>_isSupported = InitializeIsSupported();
}

private static bool IsSupported => <>_isSupported;
```
When the System.Diagnostics.Tracing.EventSource.IsSupported linker feature is set, is the linker able to unwind all of that back to just:
```C#
private static bool IsSupported => false;
```
or do we end up with:
```C#
private static readonly bool <>_isSupported;

static /*beforefieldinit*/ EventSource
{
    <>_isSupported = InitializeIsSupported();
}

private static bool IsSupported => false;
```
?

You get the latter:

```C#
        static EventSource()
        {
            EventSource.<IsSupported>k__BackingField = EventSource.InitializeIsSupported();
        }

        private static bool IsSupported
        {
            get
            {
                return false;
            }
        }
```

We discussed this a bit here: https://github.com/mono/linker/issues/1112#issuecomment-627506851. Do you think this will be an issue leaving this dead field and method?

cc @vitek-karas @MichalStrehovsky

Similarly, rather than all this indenting, could we make it be:
```C#
if (!IsSupported)
{
    return;
}
```
and leave the rest of the method untouched?

Could the changes to this method instead just be:
```C#
if (!IsSupported)
{
    return Array.Empty<EventSource>();
}
```
?
